('127.888.d.18.D',3,'A student explains why HF radio is used over oceans while VHF is limited to line of sight. She is:','["describing seats", "describing tires", "explaining the basic operation of communications systems", "avoiding radios"]'::jsonb,2,'Comm operation.','original'),
('127.888.d.18.D',4,'HF radio can travel long distances because the waves:','["go underground", "avoid air", "stop at clouds", "bounce off the ionosphere"]'::jsonb,3,'HF range.','original'),
('127.888.d.18.E',3,'A student studies an ELT''s antenna, battery, switch and 406 MHz transmitter and how it signals a crash. She is:','["identifying the components of an emergency locator transmitter and explaining its operation", "ignoring batteries", "painting an ELT", "avoiding ELTs"]'::jsonb,0,'ELT.','original'),
('127.888.d.18.E',4,'An ELT is designed to:','["boost power", "transmit a distress signal after a crash", "cool the cabin", "improve fuel flow"]'::jsonb,1,'ELT purpose.','original'),
('127.888.d.18.F',3,'A student labels a DME interrogator, ILS receiver, GPS antenna and ADF loop on a diagram. She is:','["labeling tires", "labeling lights", "identifying the components of navigation systems", "labeling seats"]'::jsonb,2,'Nav components.','original'),
('127.888.d.18.F',4,'A GPS receiver determines position using signals from:','["ground clouds", "the engine", "nearby cars", "satellites"]'::jsonb,3,'GPS.','original'),
