('127.888.d.19.D',4,'An ELT battery should be replaced when it:','["is cold", "reaches its expiration date or has been used past its limit", "is clean", "is new"]'::jsonb,1,'Battery life.','original'),
('127.888.d.19.E',3,'A mechanic follows the manual to mount an antenna, seal the base and bond it to the skin. She is:','["guessing", "ignoring the manual", "locating and explaining the installation procedures for antennas, including mounting", "painting the antenna"]'::jsonb,2,'Antenna install.','original'),
('127.888.d.19.E',4,'An antenna''s base should be sealed to prevent:','["fuel leaks", "paint wear", "signal gain", "moisture from entering the skin or fuselage"]'::jsonb,3,'Seal base.','original'),
('127.888.d.20.A',3,'A student labels a boost pump, strainer, selector valve and filter on a fuel system diagram. She is:','["identifying fuel system types and fuel system components", "labeling tires", "labeling seats", "labeling lights"]'::jsonb,0,'Fuel components.','original'),
('127.888.d.20.A',4,'A fuel selector valve allows the pilot to:','["raise the gear", "choose which tank feeds the engine", "adjust the seat", "change radio channel"]'::jsonb,1,'Selector valve.','original'),
('127.888.d.20.B',3,'A student compares rigid integral tanks in a wing with flexible bladder cells. She is:','["comparing wheels", "comparing seats", "differentiating between types of aircraft fuel tanks and fuel cells", "comparing lights"]'::jsonb,2,'Tank types.','original'),
('127.888.d.20.B',4,'An integral fuel tank is formed by:','["using a barrel", "adding a bag", "using a drum", "sealing the structure of the wing itself"]'::jsonb,3,'Integral tank.','original'),
('127.888.d.20.C',3,'A technician explains how fuel moves between tanks, from the truck to the aircraft, out of the aircraft and dumped in flight. She is:','["explaining fuel flow during transfer, fueling, defueling and jettisoning", "describing seats", "avoiding fuel", "describing tires"]'::jsonb,0,'Fuel flow.','original'),
('127.888.d.20.C',4,'Fuel jettisoning is used to:','["add weight", "reduce the aircraft''s weight in an emergency", "refuel in flight", "warm the engine"]'::jsonb,1,'Jettison.','original'),
('127.888.d.20.D',3,'A student compares avgas, Jet A and automotive fuel by their properties. She is:','["describing seats", "avoiding fuel", "describing characteristics of fuel types", "describing tires"]'::jsonb,2,'Fuel types.','original'),
('127.888.d.20.D',4,'Avgas used in piston aircraft is usually dyed:','["clear", "purple", "red", "blue (100LL)"]'::jsonb,3,'Avgas color.','original'),
('127.888.d.20.E',3,'A shop grounds the aircraft, wears protective gear and follows the manual before opening a fuel tank. She is:','["describing fuel system maintenance industry best practices", "skipping steps", "ignoring practices", "guessing"]'::jsonb,0,'Fuel best practices.','original'),
('127.888.d.20.E',4,'Grounding an aircraft before fueling prevents:','["cold fuel", "static sparks that could ignite fuel vapors", "extra lift", "extra fuel"]'::jsonb,1,'Grounding.','original'),
('127.888.d.20.F',3,'A student compares a float-type sender, a capacitance probe and an electric sender used to read fuel level. She is:','["comparing seats", "comparing lights", "differentiating between fuel quantity indication methods", "comparing wheels"]'::jsonb,2,'Quantity methods.','original'),
